cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this artifact, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "ORM overhead on four database systems: harness, results and correction register"
abstract: >-
  The artifact behind a study of what Django and SQLAlchemy cost against each
  framework's own hand-written SQL, measured on four database systems in two
  schema configurations across workloads derived from the 22 queries of TPC-H
  and the five transactions of TPC-C, at scale factor 1. It contains the
  harness, both frameworks' implementations of all 27 workloads, the analysis
  scripts that produce every table and figure in the manuscript, the resolution
  bounds fixed before the pilot ran, and a register of 46 measurement defects
  found while building and reviewing it. One system's 108 cells carry no timing:
  its developer licence forbids disclosing benchmark results for it without
  written approval. Those cells remain as rows with the reason recorded, so the
  432-cell grid stays countable. MANIFEST.md gives the full account.
